This file describes the directives and concepts tested by this test set.

test set name: gpio01

directives:

  rtems_gpio_ctrl_init
  rtems_gpio_ctrl_register
  rtems_gpio_get_info
  rtems_gpio_pin_get_info
  rtems_gpio_pin_by_name
  rtems_gpio_pin_configure
  rtems_gpio_pin_get_configuration
  rtems_gpio_pin_release
  rtems_gpio_pin_get
  rtems_gpio_pin_set
  rtems_gpio_pin_toggle
  rtems_gpio_pin_get_multiple
  rtems_gpio_pin_set_multiple
  rtems_gpio_pin_irq_enable
  rtems_gpio_pin_irq_disable

concepts:

  - A controller registers as an IMFS node and every operation is an ioctl()
    on it.

  - A pin the board reserves is refused with EACCES before the driver is
    called, and is left unconfigured by the refusal.

  - A configuration asking for something the pin does not report in its
    capabilities is refused with ENOTSUP, decided in the generic layer from
    what pin_get_info() reported.

  - A handler a driver did not implement answers ENOTSUP rather than calling
    through a null pointer.

  - A driver that rounds a value reports what it applied, both from
    rtems_gpio_pin_configure() and from rtems_gpio_pin_get_configuration().

  - An active-low pin speaks logical levels and the pad takes the opposite
    one, asserted against the simulated pad rather than against a second API
    call.

  - A multiple-pin write containing one unusable pin changes none of them.

  - Pins are logical and continuous; the controller decides what they are.
    Physical and virtual pins are both pins and differ only in what
    rtems_gpio_pin_get_info() reports.

negative control:

  Each check below was run with the code it tests removed, and the line the
  test then stopped on is recorded.  A test that has never been seen to fail
  is not evidence that the code it covers works.

    1. cpukit/dev/gpio/gpio.c, rtems_gpio_do_configure(): remove the
       RTEMS_GPIO_PIN_RESERVED check.
       -> init.c:56 "rv == -1", reached from
          test_reserved_pin_is_refused().  The pin configured.

    2. cpukit/dev/gpio/gpio.c, rtems_gpio_do_configure(): remove the
       "needed & ~info.capabilities" check.
       -> init.c:56 "rv == -1", reached from
          test_capabilities_are_enforced().  An open-drain output configured
          on a pin that has no open drain.

       1 and 2 stop on the same line because assert_fails() is shared; the
       call stack is what tells them apart.

    3. cpukit/dev/gpio/gpio.c, rtems_gpio_do_pin_set_multiple(): check the
       pins after calling pin_set_multiple() rather than before.
       -> init.c:384 "test_gpio_raw_level( TEST_GPIO_PIN_FULL ) == 1".  The
          call still returned EBADF, and two of the three pins had already
          been written.

    4. testsuites/libtests/gpio01/test_gpio.c, test_gpio_pin_configure():
       do not round drive_strength.
       -> init.c:270 "config.drive_strength == TEST_GPIO_DRIVE_STRENGTH".
